My prior call was correct in substance: the driver remains directionless. The FOMC language maintains steady accommodation with a gentle guidance toward further rate increases, acknowledging solid labor and inflation below target. This posture supports modest long-end demands but provides no urgency either way. The curve itself remains shallow historically, offering no compression shock; nor has it broken out. Copper-gold weakness is the clearest risk-off signal in the mix, but a single negative 8-week reading after months of flatness is not yet a conviction reversal. Dollar weakness is modest in magnitude.

